      "message": "Drive-by nit:\n\n`set_ac_prochot` and `charger_prochot_init` are variations of a function name that are both doing essentially the same thing.\n\n1. If only a single `CONFIG_CHARGER_` value can be enabled at a time, then these functions should all have the same name, for consistency-sake. I don\u0027t have strong feelings either way which name we should adopt.\n\n2. If multiple `CONFIG_CHARGER_` values can be enabled for the same build (which means the function names can\u0027t collide), then we should adopt a naming convention to prevent what we\u0027re seeing here. I suggest something like: `charger_prochot_init\u003ccharger name\u003e`. For the chargers we have here, the function names would be:\n    - `charger_prochot_init_ISL9241`\n    - `charger_prochot_init_ISL9238`\n\nThoughts?",
